{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet","id":1263026,"title":"Chilling Adventures of Sabrina - any opinions yet?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-10-27T00:36:13-07:00","id":1263026,"title":"Chilling Adventures of Sabrina - any opinions yet?","content":"I saw the trailer for the Netflix re-imagining of Sabrina the Teenage Witch and watched the first two episodes last night.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=ybKUX6thF8Q\" target=\"_blank\">Trailer here</a><br /> <br /> Surprisingly they're not afraid to use the S-word and there seems to be plenty of blood to hand in the sfx department and even a bit of near nudity. They seem to have thought about their version of the witch 'culture' in the writing and look like they're going to explore it too. There's also a definite 'keep our version of the world secret' thing going on.<br /> <br /> So it struck me that it might be good inspiration for World of Darkness; and then it struck me that WoD, despite being claimed as 'edgy' has a strong anti-satanic (infernal) element to it (even to these days). It seems like the 'ultimate evil' in most of the main lines are infernalists. Which, I assume, came about as a reaction to the 80s rpgs = satan worshipping scaremongering being in the minds of the creators when they started writing the game in the late 80s/early 90s and has just been carried forward without change.<br /> <br /> So a few questions: first, any opinions on Sabrina? Second, would a satan worshipping sect of sorcerers or mages be hunted down in the WoD? Third, is it time to rethink the anti infernalism components?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11490-dogstar","name":"Dogstar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11490_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"381"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-29T09:12:18-07:00","id":1263364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dogstar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet#post1263026\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Second, would a satan worshipping sect of sorcerers or mages be hunted down in the WoD?</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't know about the rest but:<br /> <br /> Vampires seem to be against infernalism (i.e: Sabbat Inquisition existing, Baali being hated). Except when they aren't (i.e: Lasombra and their Abyss worship coexisting with the Inquisition). So I guess it depends on the current state of vampire politics, but most of the time a satan worshipping sect will get the ax.<br /> <br /> In Mage the Traditions forbbide <i>worshipping and serving </i>demons but not summoning or dealing with them, so there's that. Also there's the whole &quot;your demon it's my pagan god&quot; argument that can allow a lot of demon worshipping under the radar. The biggest risk for Infernalists it's that they may be confused with Nephandi (which, ironically, ally with demons but refuse to serve them, as per M20), other than that they get the same level of hunting as other Reality Deviants (except they also have to care for the occasional holly knigth)<br /> <br /> Demons fully endorse sects worshipping them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 10-29-2018, 12:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-10-30T22:51:39-07:00","id":1263745,"title":"","content":"The setting treats Infernal and those closely allied thematically (Nephandi, Baali, Black Spiral Dancers) as the only BLACK in a very morally grey setting. <br /> Except if you factor in the Demon Splat, where Demons are still a dark shade of Grey, but Earthbound are the BLACK in comparison.<br /> <br /> I think that the world NEEDS a Black for comparison, A line in the sand that is considered too far to go for NPCs and PCs alike, where you can ally with former enemies because the antagonist is SO EVIL.<br /> <br /> It also makes playing the darker stuff more... difficult. Sure Abyss Mysticism is _arguably_ bad, but it's definitively, &quot;Not as Bad as the Infernal&quot; so it's easier to bring into a game, because you can see that it's not all bad (Works for In game and Out of Game rationale) <br /> <br /> Even the mention of there being sort-of-good (or less bad) Baali in the second Black Hand Book. They apparently are Demonologists, not Infernalists; so they're ok. I personally think that the faction may have fooled many, including most of the young of their own clan/faction; But they're still as evil as actually selling your soul because they are doing horrific things to keep the Demons asleep.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/The_Black_Hand:_A_Guide_to_the_Tal%E2%80%99Mahe%E2%80%99Ra\" target=\"_blank\">https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Th...ahe%E2%80%99Ra</a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T03:00:01-07:00","id":1263999,"title":"","content":"I think you could easily swap in the whole &quot;Demons are just Pagan Gods&quot; angle and while I'm only a couple episodes in these people aren't &quot;WOD infernalists&quot; They aren't Nihilist true believers they are just kind of petty assholes. Honestly its more &quot;Good Omens&quot; satanism than anything","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T11:36:15-07:00","id":1264086,"title":"","content":"Hurmm....too infernalist to work as mage per say. <br /> <br /> I mean, the concept and the way magick works in interesting and solid nough BUUUT....its closer to nephandi than verbena","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Forum's Official's Joker and Trickster. Pardon my bad english, aint my first language (I Speak Spanish).<br /> ST: DtF, HtR, WtO, MtA<br /> Signature Chars: Crowley (hakalu), Joe The Nuwisha (WtA)<br /> Changelings: be afraid of the Technocracian High Five of Doom","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1754-crowley","name":"Crowley","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1754_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1639"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T15:38:50-07:00","id":1264144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1263999#post1263999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could easily swap in the whole &quot;Demons are just Pagan Gods&quot; angle and while I'm only a couple episodes in these people aren't &quot;WOD infernalists&quot; They aren't Nihilist true believers they are just kind of petty assholes. Honestly its more &quot;Good Omens&quot; satanism than anything</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if they are worshipping a &quot;Pagan God&quot; they literally believe that he is Lucifer, Satan. In a couple of episode's time they read from the bible and talk about how the &quot;False God&quot; traps mortals<br /> They get powers from the Devil, Signing their soul over to him, and (Things the call) literal devils exist. And all of that is up front by episode 2","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-01T20:13:27-07:00","id":1264190,"title":"","content":"It may be of interest to note that nothing of that's really Nephandic <i>per se -</i> not after Crusade separated Nephandi Infernalists from &quot;just&quot; Infernalists.<br /> <br /> However, worshipping the devil and, worse, selling your soul to him it's NOT kosher within the Traditions. A group like that would get the ax from the Traditions on top of the hunting mages already suffer if they don't have the decorum of calling their Lucifer some other name when Heralds comes to visit (and you may also want to hidde under the carpet all that dark ressonance while you're at it).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-01-2018, 11:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T05:25:17-07:00","id":1264249,"title":"","content":"I thought the ideology/religion of Sabrina was a bit of a mess. Like, they're evil, frequently cannibalistic witches who sign their souls over to Satan (this is normal and casually accepted among witches), but they are shocked by hazing rituals, care about children, trap or destroy demons (surely on their side?), and are very inconsistent about whether murder is evil or not (Zelda says, 'So you're a murderer now?' despite having killed Hilda several times herself!).<br /> <br /> Honestly, they needed someone with an understanding of the occult and various mythologies to make this work. Satanism as a kind of mystical libertarianism would work (look at the actual Church of Satan); or Satanism as a kind of defiant, feminist mysticism a la the Bahari; or even Baali-esque infernalism-to-placate-demons would all have worked better than what they gave us.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-02T13:32:53-07:00","id":1264323,"title":"","content":"I haven't seen the series, but it's by the same creator as the comic and I found the witches' culture in the latter to be largely incoherent. There's lip service to the stereotypical trappings of being eeevil devil worshipers, but the same people who are performing black masses largely live and relate to each other like image-conscious suburbanites from the 1950s.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T13:45:52-07:00","id":1264491,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1264144#post1264144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even if they are worshipping a &quot;Pagan God&quot; they literally believe that he is Lucifer, Satan. In a couple of episode's time they read from the bible and talk about how the &quot;False God&quot; traps mortals<br /> They get powers from the Devil, Signing their soul over to him, and (Things the call) literal devils exist. And all of that is up front by episode 2</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> IT is.. but it isn't. They basically are Satanists like the Satanists in Good Omens. Its just trappings. While you couldn't word for word swap them out into the Traditions you wouldn't change much if you called the Dark Lord the Horned Lord and went with &quot;Witches are Pagans&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T18:17:34-07:00","id":1264535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1264249#post1264249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the ideology/religion of Sabrina was a bit of a mess. Like, they're evil, frequently cannibalistic witches who sign their souls over to Satan (this is normal and casually accepted among witches), but they are shocked by hazing rituals, care about children, trap or destroy demons (surely on their side?), and are very inconsistent about whether murder is evil or not (Zelda says, 'So you're a murderer now?' despite having killed Hilda several times herself!).<br /> <br /> Honestly, they needed someone with an understanding of the occult and various mythologies to make this work. Satanism as a kind of mystical libertarianism would work (look at the actual Church of Satan); or Satanism as a kind of defiant, feminist mysticism a la the Bahari; or even Baali-esque infernalism-to-placate-demons would all have worked better than what they gave us.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yup, but you can't make those into protagonists in a show on Netflix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, I agree, they muddied/handwaved things to be able to make witches edgy and appealingly dark, but still be able to have nice, good witches.<br /> <br /> Though, despite all that, I found the show enjoyable.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-03T20:41:17-07:00","id":1264556,"title":"","content":"The Church of Night is basically a pisstake of Fundamentalist High-Control Christian Denominations. Hell the language used, especially by <span style=\"color:#545454\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Faustus Blackwood, is word for word what I hear on Sundays and Wednesdays.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-08T05:32:23-08:00","id":1265492,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1264535#post1264535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yup, but you can't make those into protagonists in a show on Netflix. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Yes, I agree, they muddied/handwaved things to be able to make witches edgy and appealingly dark, but still be able to have nice, good witches.<br /> <br /> Though, despite all that, I found the show enjoyable.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was made more complicated by just inverting things. So demonic judges are 'dishonours' (though the witches still seem to think honour is good, so why would this be a term of respect?) and 'evil' words are subbed in simply for 'good' words.<br /> <br /> But I do like the show. I just wish they'd cleaned up the mythos first (even if it is a satire of RL patriarchal religion).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T03:06:18-08:00","id":1268502,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1263999#post1263999\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you could easily swap in the whole &quot;Demons are just Pagan Gods&quot; angle and while I'm only a couple episodes in these people aren't &quot;WOD infernalists&quot; They aren't Nihilist true believers they are just kind of petty assholes. Honestly its more &quot;Good Omens&quot; satanism than anything</div> </div> </div> </div>But the games make quite a distinct line between dark gods (and quite a few splats are anything but squeamish about their practices) and entities inimical to human existence. Infernalists and BSD's traffic and serve those. The Nephandi are inimical to human existence and think themselves better then these entities, but commonly engage with them.<br /> <br /> So it's not about nomenclature in the WOD, it's about what they do. If Satan is really about corruption, debasement and servitude he's on the naughty list. Now if he's actually a fallen angel fighting against a corrupt God and seeiking to bring Wisdom to humanityhe might be on the nice list. The best thing about WOD is that there is room for both of these, and either of them masking as the other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T06:31:09-08:00","id":1268531,"title":"","content":"It depicts all Witches by equating their religion and practices to Satanism and WICCAN is just an acronym for a feminist power group. Being that my WICCAN friends who if you did not know are also known as witches struggle each day to try to get rid of these blatant stereotypes. Also if you didn't know its stereo types like this that spur hatred towards their religion. Funny story I was once hit in the head with a bible because I was Wiccan, I do prefer it to when I got stabbed because &quot;thou shall not suffer a witch to live&quot; or to the lesser extent when some of my children could not wear their pentacles because the school decided that just those items not crosses or red bandanas were gang signs and the school had a policy against wearing gang signs or the time my mother cried out &quot;your a witch!&quot; when I tried to tell her about my religion in a restaurant and then ran from me like I was Satan himself. Some of the patrons of the restaurant were religious and this is what led to me getting beaten in a ally latter that night.<br /> <br /> That being said I think it is alright for a work of fiction but remember it is just that and not an actual depiction of Witches or Wiccans or there real world struggle nor is it an excuse to cause real world hate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11720,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","user":"Redwulfe","date":". 11-18-2018, 10:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11720-redwulfe","name":"Redwulfe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11720_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"570"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:30:20-08:00","id":1269052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Asmodai</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1268502#post1268502\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But the games make quite a distinct line between dark gods (and quite a few splats are anything but squeamish about their practices) and entities inimical to human existence. Infernalists and BSD's traffic and serve those. The Nephandi are inimical to human existence and think themselves better then these entities, but commonly engage with them.<br /> <br /> So it's not about nomenclature in the WOD, it's about what they do. If Satan is really about corruption, debasement and servitude he's on the naughty list. Now if he's actually a fallen angel fighting against a corrupt God and seeiking to bring Wisdom to humanityhe might be on the nice list. The best thing about WOD is that there is room for both of these, and either of them masking as the other <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And Sabrina isn't set in the World of Darkness? ITs abit incoherent about the morality of the setting but GENERALLY the Church of night functions as if you swap the names around on the dickish end of the Traditions and not the Full on NEphandi/infernalist Cult/etc level of shit. They don't act particular debased. They aren't working on destroying the world. They aren't even spreading evil just hiding from the mortals.<br /> <br /> Its not bad inspiration for the Order of Hermes, or Clan Tremere... but they aren't even Sabbat or Settite Hard Core monsters...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T07:15:41-08:00","id":1269218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1264249#post1264249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought the ideology/religion of Sabrina was a bit of a mess. Like, they're evil, frequently cannibalistic witches who sign their souls over to Satan (this is normal and casually accepted among witches), but they are shocked by hazing rituals, care about children, trap or destroy demons (surely on their side?), and are very inconsistent about whether murder is evil or not (Zelda says, 'So you're a murderer now?' despite having killed Hilda several times herself!).</div> </div> </div> </div>I actually got the feeling that was intentional and part of the show's humor, the general campy scenery devouring Satanism (always saying &quot;praise Satan&quot; whenever something good happens) particularly the whole nightmare sequence where they basically did a complete inversion of the Cain and Abel story with Hilda and Zelda is what confirmed this for me in my mind. It's pretty clear this show never set out to be a serious take on Satanism. And that's fine with me.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Redwulfe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1263026-chilling-adventures-of-sabrina-any-opinions-yet?p=1268531#post1268531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It depicts all Witches by equating their religion and practices to Satanism and WICCAN is just an acronym for a feminist power group. Being that my WICCAN friends who if you did not know are also known as witches struggle each day to try to get rid of these blatant stereotypes. Also if you didn't know its stereo types like this that spur hatred towards their religion. Funny story I was once hit in the head with a bible because I was Wiccan, I do prefer it to when I got stabbed because &amp;quot;thou shall not suffer a witch to live&amp;quot; or to the lesser extent when some of my children could not wear their pentacles because the school decided that just those items not crosses or red bandanas were gang signs and the school had a policy against wearing gang signs or the time my mother cried out &amp;quot;your a witch!&amp;quot; when I tried to tell her about my religion in a restaurant and then ran from me like I was Satan himself. Some of the patrons of the restaurant were religious and this is what led to me getting beaten in a ally latter that night.<br /> <br /> That being said I think it is alright for a work of fiction but remember it is just that and not an actual depiction of Witches or Wiccans or there real world struggle nor is it an excuse to cause real world hate.</div> </div> </div> </div>Duly noted and understood. I'm sorry you and other wiccans deal with that sort of nonsense all the time, I live in the Bible belt and hide that I follow certain occult traditions myself, so I avoid most of the assaults, but it does make one feel isolated after a while.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":20546,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","user":"Dragonchild","date":". 11-20-2018, 10:23 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/20546-dragonchild","name":"Dragonchild","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}